/// Copies the first half-word of the status block into the state word at
/// `+0x0C`, then for each of the three pending bits (`+8` bits 3/2/5 against
/// `+0x0C` bits 1/0/4) updates the state and its 16-bit mirror: bit 3 resumes
/// the queue and clears the pending count, bit 2 raises the pending count and
/// resumes, bit 5 clears the bit and calls the completion callback bracketed by
/// the context save/restore pair.
///
/// # Safety
